    "https://cobleskill.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205654": {
      "title": "Baker/Prep Supervisor Non-Union - CAS Dining Services at",
      "description": "SUNY Cobleskill\nJob Posting: Baker/Prep Supervisor Non-Union - CAS Dining Services at SUNY Cobleskill SUNY Cobleskill \n\tJob Posting: Baker/Prep Supervisor Non-Union - CAS Dining Services at SUNY Cobleskill Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Baker/Prep Supervisor Non-Union - CAS Dining Services at SUNY Cobleskill Category: CAS Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: CAS Locations: Cobleskill, NY Posted: Oct 9, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 205654 Share About SUNY Cobleskill: SUNY Cobleskill Auxiliary Services, (CAS) is a not-for-profit corporation committed to delivering quality services at competitive prices to the SUNY Cobleskill campus community.  CAS Provides outstanding services that collectively support students, faculty, staff, and guests while contributing to the local community.  Through expert customer service, CAS supports the pursuit of academic excellence, encourages personal growth, and cultivates sustainability, yielding superior quality of life for all. Job Description: The Production & Bakery Supervisor will accurately and efficiently prepare, portion, cook, and present a variety of hot and/or cold food/desserts, breads and other baked items for various meal periods: to include Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner, and Special/Catered Events. Will be able to open and close the dining hall and other retail operations. The general responsibilities of the position include those listed below but may identify other responsibilities of the position. These responsibilities may differ according to business necessities and client requirements. General Responsibilities: Assumes responsibilities of Supervisor Baker, is responsible to address, problem solve and interact effectively and autonomously respectively to the preparation and delivery of the Bakery Items. Leads and directs the team to include the Union & Non-Union along with Students. Responsible to schedule and staff all baking back of the house employees in an efficient manner. Responsible to partner with Executive Chef and Catering Director to minimize labor costs. Prepares food by operating a variety of kitchen equipment to measure and mix ingredients, washing, peeling, cutting and shredding fruits and vegetables, for use. Provides the highest quality of service to customers at all times. Tastes products, reads menus, estimates food requirements, check production, and keep records in order to accurately plan production requirements and requisition supplies and equipment. Orders products and keeps inventory. Clean and sanitize workstations and equipment and must follow all client and regulatory rules and procedures. Attend all allergy and foodborne illness in-service training, ServSafe Certified. Comply with all HACCP policies and procedures. Reports all accidents and injuries in a timely manner. Complies with all company safety and risk management policies and procedures. Participate in regular safety meetings, safety trainings and hazard assessments. Attends training programs (classroom and virtual), as designated. Produces small to large batch goods using advanced and full range of classical and contemporary cooking, plating and garnishing techniques. Follows complex recipes and/or product directions for preparing, seasoning, cooking, tasting desserts and other foodstuffs for consumption in eating establishments. Assist with the supervision of kitchen personnel and front-of-the-house staff. Selects recipes per menu cycle, prepares bakery items, receives inventory, moves and lifts foodstuffs and supplies, and prepares meals for customers requiring special diets. Serves as a lead baker guiding and assisting in the training of less-experienced bakers, including union staff and students. Under minimal supervision, independently performs advanced cooking duties in preparing food items to be served to customers. Advanced knife skills required. May have oversight over the production staff and assign tasks. May use production software to enter pre- and post-production data software. May take inventory, and/or enter inventory into the \"system\" used to record, as required. May perform other duties and responsibilities as assigned. Requirements: 4 years Baking experience a must. Knowledge of basic operation of equipment and product ordering and inventory. Experience/Knowledge: Presents self in a highly professional manner to others and understands that honesty and ethics are essential. Ability to maintain a positive attitude. Ability to communicate with co-workers and other departments with professionalism and respect, using good judgement and behavior with a positive attitude. Maintains a professional relationship with all coworkers, vendor representatives, supervisors, managers, customers, and client representatives, as well as the campus community. Ability to use a computer. Must be able to read and follow a recipe, unsupervised Involved with the more complex requirements of the position. Applies advanced cooking skills. Adapts procedures, processes, tools, equipment and techniques to meet the requirements of the position. Substantial working knowledge of food preparation. Willingness to be open to learning and growing. Maintains high standards for work areas and appearance. Ability to work a flexible schedule. Must comply with any dress code requirements. Must be able to work nights, weekends and some holidays. Attends work and shows up for scheduled shift on time with satisfactory regularity. Physical Requirements: Ability to work in a standing position for long periods of time (up to 8 hours). Ability to reach, bend, stand, push and/or pull, and frequently lift to 50 pounds and occasionally lift/move 50 pounds. Generally, in an indoor setting; however, may supervise outside activities and events. Varying schedule to include evenings, holidays, weekends and extended hours as business dictates. While performing the duties of this job, the employee is primarily in a controlled, temperate environment; however, may be exposed to heat/cold during support of outside activities. The noise level in the work environment is usually moderate to loud. Additional Information: Hours:  Full-time, Non-Union Sunday, 7:30am - 3:30 pm Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, 5:00 am - 1:00 pm Hourly, Non-Exempt, 37.5 hours/week, (coincides with the academic calendar) 40-weeks per year Based on experience $20.00 - $24.00/hour EEO STATEMENT: EEO employees are protected by federal laws, Presidential Executive Orders and other laws from discrimination on the basis of race, religion, color, sex (including pregnancy and gender identity), sexual orientation, parental status, national origin, age, disability, family medical history or genetic information, political affiliations, military service or any other non-merit-based factors.  These protections extend to all management practices and decisions, including recruitment and hiring practices, appraisal systems, promotions, and training and career development programs.  EEO employees are also protected against retaliation.  Consistent with federal laws, acts of retaliation against an employee who engages in a protected activity, whistle blowing, or the exercise of any appeal or grievance right provided by law, will not be tolerated.  In addition, consistent with the RESOLVED Program (Non-Retaliation Statement9, the EEOC will not tolerate retaliation against participation in RESOLVE. EEOC managers and supervisors are also reminded again of their responsibility to prevent, document and promptly address/correct harassing conduct in the workplace. Application Instructions: The application review process will begin immediately and will continue until a suitable candidate is found. Please provide: Resume Cover Letter References Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Cobleskill 106 Suffolk Circle, Cobleskill, NY 12043"
