    "https://cobleskill.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205815": {
      "title": "Program Coordinator -",
      "description": "SUNY Cobleskill\nJob Posting: Program Coordinator - SUNY Cobleskill Liberty Partnerships Program - Research Foundation SUNY Cobleskill \n\tJob Posting: Program Coordinator - SUNY Cobleskill Liberty Partnerships Program - Research Foundation Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Program Coordinator - SUNY Cobleskill Liberty Partnerships Program - Research Foundation Category: Staff Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Research Foundation Locations: Cobleskill, NY Posted: Oct 15, 2026 Closes: Nov 15, 2026 - 11:59 PM EST Type: Full-time Position ID: 205815 Share About SUNY Cobleskill: The State University of New York College of Agriculture and Technology at Cobleskill is an accredited polytechnic college that is primarily baccalaureate and residential. SUNY Cobleskill is one of few institutions in the United States where an undergraduate student may also choose to earn an associate degree. The College has an enrollment of approximately 2,500 students in 59 programs divided into two schools, Agriculture and Natural Resources; Business and Liberal Arts & Sciences. An economic engine for rural New York, SUNY Cobleskill is home to a wide array of extended learning and professional development opportunities. Modeling experiential education, SUNY Cobleskill is committed to providing small classes, excellent facilities, and a hands-on learning environment. Whether students plan to further their education or begin their professional careers, they graduate with the foundation to pursue their goals and to succeed. Job Description: This position is offered by the SUNY Research Foundation, which is located on the SUNY Cobleskill campus.  Employment is not affiliated with the State of New York or the State University of New York. The SUNY Research Foundation is a private not-for-profit entity that administers research projects for SUNY campuses, http://www.rfsuny.org/. The SUNY Cobleskill Liberty Partnerships Program (LPP) is a New York State Education Dept. grant-funded dropout prevention program serving youth in grades 6 through 12, and their families, in 6 school districts within Schoharie, Otsego, and Delaware Counties. LPP partners with the SUNY Research Foundation to administer this grant.  This position will be located on the campus of SUNY Cobleskill.  This is a 12-month, 30-hours-per-week position. The SUNY Cobleskill Liberty Partnerships Program is looking for an energetic, personable, and highly organized individual to fill the position of Program Coordinator and become part of a team of professionals who strive to ensure that program participants successfully graduate high school and enter post-secondary education and/or the workforce as highly competent young adults. Responsibilities: Arrange college and career exploration experiences for LPP students, such as field trips and job shadows Attend and assist in student supervision during trips, both on and off campus Drive SUNY fleet vehicles, such as 7-passenger and 12-passenger vans, to transport students and staff, as needed. Take and pass the SUNY Cobleskill Van Safety Course Complete any and all professional development required by the State, the college, and the LPP Director Support the work of LPP Advocates in the schools, including the purchase and delivery of supplies, as needed Office tasks, such as data entry, filing, making copies, and organizing Utilize social media to promote and celebrate LPP events Perform other job-related duties as assigned by the LPP Director to further the mission of the Liberty Partnerships Program Requirements: A minimum of an Bachelor's degree A minimum of 1 years' experience in an office or school setting. Experience planning events is a plus. Strong communication and interpersonal skills Must be organized and detail oriented Must have a valid Driver's License Experience with Microsoft Word and Excel Available to work the occasional evening or weekend event Additional Information: This is a full-time, full calendar year position (37.5 hours/week) The starting hourly wage range is $21 per hour Research Foundation for SUNY offers exceptional benefits such as healthcare, dental, vision, pension plans, competitive pay, generous paid time off, tuition assistance, life insurance and long-term disability insurance. As an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer, Research Foundation for SUNY at SUNY Cobleskill will not discriminate in its employment practices due to an applicant's race, creed, religion, color, citizenship, national origin, sex, age, sexual orientation, predisposing genetic characteristics, gender identification or expression, genetic information, familial status, marital status, pregnancy, status as a domestic violence victim, recently separated veteran, or other characteristics as protected by law. Please feel free to review your equal employment opportunities protections and laws pertaining to these protections at http://www.dol.gov/ofccp/regs/compliance/posters/pdf/eeopost.pdf. Application Instructions: The application review process will begin immediately and will continue until a suitable candidate is found. A complete application consists of the following: A resume outlining education and work experience A cover letter stating how your education and work experience relates to the job responsibilities outlined above Three professional references *To apply, you must create an account and apply through this posting. The Research Foundation for The State University of New York, an EEO/AA/IRCA/ADA employer, offers exceptional benefits such as healthcare, dental, vision, pension plans, competitive pay, generous paid time off, tuition assistance, life insurance and long-term disability insurance. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Cobleskill 106 Suffolk Circle, Cobleskill, NY 12043"
    },
    "https://cobleskill.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205581": {
      "title": "Graphic Designer",
      "description": "SUNY Cobleskill\nJob Posting: Graphic Designer SUNY Cobleskill \n\tJob Posting: Graphic Designer Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Graphic Designer Category: Staff Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Communications and Marketing Locations: Cobleskill, NY Posted: Oct 7, 2026 Closes: Nov 4, 2026 - 11:59 PM EST Type: Full-time Temporary Position ID: 205581 Share About SUNY Cobleskill: As New York's leading public college for agriculture and technology, SUNY Cobleskill Ag & Tech develops students who wish to positively impact the future well-being of human society and sustainable practices. Our immersive approach to learning combines academic rigor with hands-on application, producing graduates who enter their careers with proven real-world capabilities. Students thrive on our 900-acre campus, providing a dynamic rural setting with a working farm, modern laboratories, and natural ecosystems serving as our classrooms. As members of this close-knit community, students gain a sense of belonging and support for lifelong learning and professional growth through direct interaction with expert faculty and industry leaders. An anchor institution in the Mohawk Valley region, the College promotes economic growth through its Institute for Rural Vitality and an extensive network of community, statewide, and national partners. We actively strengthen the industries that align with our academic programs and mission by providing modern business resources, training, and technical assistance while offering shared-use facilities that support regional entrepreneurs, creating new connections for sustainable development. Drawing on a rich academic tradition that spans more than 100 years, our purpose remains constant: to educate and support undergraduate learners and researchers to be workforce-ready and affect the two most significant forces in today's world - agriculture and technology. Job Description: SUNY Cobleskill Ag & Tech is looking for a Digital Graphic Designer to join our Marketing Team. This role requires a high degree of digital literacy and experience to support the development of high-quality advertising, marketing and other collateral materials across a variety of mediums in order to keep the SUNY Cobleskill Ag & Tech at the forefront of our audiences' minds when it comes to making us their higher education choice. Key Responsibilities: Coordinating graphic design projects and campaigns with stakeholders, generating clear ideas, concepts, and designs of creative assets from beginning to end The design of digital and print assets for organic and paid advertising created in Adobe Creative Suite (Examples: digital display ads, social media posts, College viewbook, etc.) Preparing and sizing digital and print files correctly to different specifications Collaboration with team members on multi-faceted projects including the ongoing development and oversight of our brand guidelines to ensure a consistent, integrated brand perception Saving and maintaining organized design files, folders, and libraries Partnering on the administration of Canva (or other related software) for departments across campus, designing in Canva when needed, saving and sharing assets Photography support Requirements: Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. If you currently need sponsorship or will need it in the future to maintain employment authorization, you do not meet eligibility requirements. Additionally, please note that SUNY Cobleskill is not an E-Verify employer. Bachelor's Degree or equivalent combination of education and experience Demonstrated grasp of color, typography, design principles/layout Strong command of Adobe Creative Suite (Cloud) products such as InDesign, Illustrator, and Photoshop A varied portfolio that highlights aesthetic awareness and design problem solving abilities including concepts, original design, and the ability to expand designs into a range of assets while adhering brand guidelines Excellent communication skills including ability to explain design decisions The ability to receive, interpret, and integrate constructive feedback back into design Able to learn new tools and processes in an ever-changing design environment Graphics animation, HTML and Photography skills a plus Additional Information: The salary for this position is $54,090.00 per year. This is a full-time, temporary appointment. This position offers full New York State benefits which are some of the most comprehensive in the country. SUNY Cobleskill is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community for our students and employees. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final candidates being considered for employment. Any offer of employment is contingent on the successful completion of the background check. This position may be designated 55 b/c and is subject to verification of applicant eligibility. All people with disabilities are encouraged to apply, if your skillset meets the minimum requirements as set forth. SUNY Cobleskill is committed to fostering a diverse community of outstanding faculty, staff, and students, and ensuring equal educational and employment opportunity and access to services, programs and activities without regard to an individual's race, color, national origin, religion, creed, age, disability, sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, familial status, pregnancy, predisposing genetic characteristics, military status, domestic violence victim status, criminal conviction, or any other legally protected status.  Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodation during the hiring process should contact the Human Resources Office at (518) 255-5514. SUNY Cobleskill's Interim Title IX Coordinator is Nicole Field, who can be contacted via phone at 518-255-5514, email at fieldnm@cobleskill.edu, or mailing address of SUNY Cobleskill,  Knapp Hall Room 123, Cobleskill, NY 12043. If you have any questions regarding this position, please contact humanresources@cobleskill.edu or 518-255-5423. Application Instructions: The application review process will begin immediately and will continue until a suitable candidate is found. Priority is given to applications submitted by November 4, 2026. A complete application consists of the following: 1. Letter of application, addressing qualifications, position responsibilities, and college values 2. Current CV or Resume 3. Names, emails and phone numbers of at least three professional references, preferably former supervisors * To apply you must create an account and apply through this posting. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Cobleskill 106 Suffolk Circle, Cobleskill, NY 12043"
    },
    "https://cobleskill.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205107": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty in Information Technology & Cybersecurity Continuous Recruitment",
      "description": "SUNY Cobleskill\nJob Posting: Adjunct Faculty in Information Technology & Cybersecurity Continuous Recruitment SUNY Cobleskill \n\tJob Posting: Adjunct Faculty in Information Technology & Cybersecurity Continuous Recruitment Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Adjunct Faculty in Information Technology & Cybersecurity Continuous Recruitment Category: Adjunct Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Information Technology & Cybersecurity Locations: Cobleskill, NY Posted: Sep 23, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Temporary Position ID: 205107 Share About SUNY Cobleskill: As New York's leading public college for agriculture and technology, SUNY Cobleskill Ag & Tech develops students who wish to positively impact the future well-being of human society and sustainable practices. Our immersive approach to learning combines academic rigor with hands-on application, producing graduates who enter their careers with proven real-world capabilities. Students thrive on our 900-acre campus, providing a dynamic rural setting with a working farm, modern laboratories, and natural ecosystems serving as our classrooms. As members of this close-knit community, students gain a sense of belonging and support for lifelong learning and professional growth through direct interaction with expert faculty and industry leaders. An anchor institution in the Mohawk Valley region, the College promotes economic growth through its Institute for Rural Vitality and an extensive network of community, statewide, and national partners. We actively strengthen the industries that align with our academic programs and mission by providing modern business resources, training, and technical assistance while offering shared-use facilities that support regional entrepreneurs, creating new connections for sustainable development. Drawing on a rich academic tradition that spans more than 100 years, our purpose remains constant: to educate and support undergraduate learners and researchers to be workforce-ready and affect the two most significant forces in today's world - agriculture and technology. Job Description: SUNY Cobleskill regularly seeks highly qualified ADJUNCT FACULTY to teach day, evening, and weekend courses in both in person and online formats within our Information Technology and Cybersecurity programs. Courses within these programs are explained in more detail in our most recent college catalog . The successful candidate will augment our faculty in the Information Technology and Cybersecurity programs and become part of a dedicated team focused on providing rich and meaningful educational experiences for our students. Requirements: Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. If you currently need sponsorship or will need it in the future to maintain employment authorization, you do not meet eligibility requirements. Additionally, please note that SUNY Cobleskill is not an E-Verify employer. A Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Information Science, Information Technology, or a closely related field from an accredited University (MS or PhD preferred). A commitment to teaching excellence and student success is essential. Prior teaching experience is preferred, however, all new adjunct faculty will be mentored. Additional Information: The College continuously recruits for applicants interested in Adjunct Faculty positions. Vacancies are determined on a semester by semester basis, and may or may not be available for the current academic semester. We invite applicants interested in current or future opportunities to submit their credentials by following the instructions noted in the Application Instructions section. Potential areas of course coverage may include those related to computer programming, networking, web development, databases, data analysis and visualization, cybersecurity, health IT, digital agriculture, sustainable computing, rural computing, and others. If you have an interest in on-campus and/or online adjunct teaching, consider SUNY Cobleskill! SUNY Cobleskill is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community for our students and employees. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final candidates being considered for employment. Any offer of employment is contingent on the successful completion of the background check. This position may be designated 55 b/c and is subject to verification of applicant eligibility. All people with disabilities are encouraged to apply, if your skillset meets the minimum requirements as set forth. SUNY Cobleskill is committed to fostering a diverse community of outstanding faculty, staff, and students, and ensuring equal educational and employment opportunity and access to services, programs and activities without regard to an individual's race, color, national origin, religion, creed, age, disability, sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, familial status, pregnancy, predisposing genetic characteristics, military status, domestic violence victim status, criminal conviction, or any other legally protected status.  Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodation during the hiring process should contact the Human Resources Office at (518) 255-5514. SUNY Cobleskill's Interim Title IX Coordinator is Nicole Field, who can be contacted via phone at 518-255-5514, email at fieldnm@cobleskill.edu, or mailing address of SUNY Cobleskill,  Knapp Hall Room 123, Cobleskill, NY 12043. If you have any questions regarding this position, please contact humanresources@cobleskill.edu or 518-255-5423. Application Instructions: This is a continuous recruitment posting. A complete application consists of the following: 1. Letter of application, addressing qualifications, position responsibilities, and college values 2. Current CV or Resume 3. Names, emails and phone numbers of at least three professional references, preferably former supervisors * To apply you must create an account and apply through this posting. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Cobleskill 106 Suffolk Circle, Cobleskill, NY 12043"
    },
    "https://cobleskill.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204528": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty in Plant Science - Continuous Recruitment",
      "description": "SUNY Cobleskill\nJob Posting: Adjunct Faculty in Plant Science - Continuous Recruitment SUNY Cobleskill \n\tJob Posting: Adjunct Faculty in Plant Science - Continuous Recruitment Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Adjunct Faculty in Plant Science - Continuous Recruitment Category: Adjunct Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Fisheries Wildlife, Env & Plant Sci Locations: Cobleskill, NY Posted: Sep 4, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Temporary Position ID: 204528 Share About SUNY Cobleskill: As New York's leading public college for agriculture and technology, SUNY Cobleskill Ag & Tech develops students who wish to positively impact the future well-being of human society and sustainable practices. Our immersive approach to learning combines academic rigor with hands-on application, producing graduates who enter their careers with proven real-world capabilities. Students thrive on our 900-acre campus, providing a dynamic rural setting with a working farm, modern laboratories, and natural ecosystems serving as our classrooms. As members of this close-knit community, students gain a sense of belonging and support for lifelong learning and professional growth through direct interaction with expert faculty and industry leaders. An anchor institution in the Mohawk Valley region, the College promotes economic growth through its Institute for Rural Vitality and an extensive network of community, statewide, and national partners. We actively strengthen the industries that align with our academic programs and mission by providing modern business resources, training, and technical assistance while offering shared-use facilities that support regional entrepreneurs, creating new connections for sustainable development. Drawing on a rich academic tradition that spans more than 100 years, our purpose remains constant: to educate and support undergraduate learners and researchers to be workforce-ready and affect the two most significant forces in today's world - agriculture and technology. Job Description: SUNY Cobleskill is seeking qualified, capable, and enthusiastic adjunct instructors to teach plant science courses. Courses may include, but are not limited to: Arboriculture Intermediate Floral Design Applied Plant Physiology Plant Propagation Botany Bonsai Full descriptions of the courses may be found here . Requirements: Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. If you currently need sponsorship or will need it in the future to maintain employment authorization, you do not meet eligibility requirements. Additionally, please note that SUNY Cobleskill is not an E-Verify employer. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's Degree in Plant Science, Horticulture or Soil Science Ability to lift 50 pounds and walk measurable distances Preferred Qualifications In addition to the aforementioned minimum qualifications, it is preferred the candidate also have: Previous, successful college teaching experience Laboratory teaching experience Master's degree or higher in Plant Science, Soil Science, Cannabis/Hemp Production or similar. Additional Information: Courses run on a 15-week academic calendar. These positions are part-time and temporary. SUNY Cobleskill is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community for our students and employees. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final candidates being considered for employment. Any offer of employment is contingent on the successful completion of the background check. This position may be designated 55 b/c and is subject to verification of applicant eligibility. All people with disabilities are encouraged to apply, if your skillset meets the minimum requirements as set forth. SUNY Cobleskill is committed to fostering a diverse community of outstanding faculty, staff, and students, and ensuring equal educational and employment opportunity and access to services, programs and activities without regard to an individual's race, color, national origin, religion, creed, age, disability, sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, familial status, pregnancy, predisposing genetic characteristics, military status, domestic violence victim status, criminal conviction, or any other legally protected status.  Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodation during the hiring process should contact the Human Resources Office at (518) 255-5514. SUNY Cobleskill's Interim Title IX Coordinator is Nicole Field, who can be contacted via phone at 518-255-5514, email at fieldnm@cobleskill.edu, or mailing address of SUNY Cobleskill,  Knapp Hall Room 123, Cobleskill, NY 12043. If you have any questions regarding this position, please contact humanresources@cobleskill.edu or 518-255-5423. Application Instructions: The application review process will begin immediately and will continue until a suitable candidate is found. A complete application consists of the following: 1. Letter of application, addressing qualifications, position responsibilities, and college values 2. Current CV or Resume 3. Names, emails and phone numbers of at least three professional references, preferably former supervisors * To apply you must create an account and apply through this posting. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Cobleskill 106 Suffolk Circle, Cobleskill, NY 12043"
    },
    "https://cobleskill.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=202457": {
      "title": "Food Handler Plus - CAS Campus Receiver - #671",
      "description": "SUNY Cobleskill\nJob Posting: Food Handler Plus - CAS Campus Receiver - #671 SUNY Cobleskill \n\tJob Posting: Food Handler Plus - CAS Campus Receiver - #671 Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Food Handler Plus - CAS Campus Receiver - #671 Category: CAS Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: CAS Locations: Cobleskill, NY Posted: Jul 10, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 202457 Share About SUNY Cobleskill: SUNY Cobleskill Auxiliary Services, (CAS) is a not-for-profit corporation committed to delivering quality services at competitive prices to the SUNY Cobleskill campus community.  CAS Provides outstanding services that collectively support students, faculty, staff, and guests while contributing to the local community.  Through expert customer service, CAS supports the pursuit of academic excellence, encourages personal growth, and cultivates sustainability, yielding superior quality of life for all. Job Description: Job Summary Reports to both Directors in Retail and Residential Dining and Senior Director of Dining Services. Responsible for receiving and inspecting food deliveries at all CAS operated locations, maintaining inventory, stocking supplies, and performing routine preventive maintenance on food service equipment to ensure safe, efficient, and uninterrupted kitchen operations. Ensure compliance with food safety, sanitation, and workplace safety standards. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Food Service Receiving Receive and inspect all food, beverages, and supply deliveries. Verify quantities, quality, expiration dates, and temperatures of delivered products. Compare deliveries against purchase orders, requisitions and invoices, checking for accuracy (pack size, quantity requested, and correct item codes). Process and copy all invoices and submit them immediately to the Dining Services Accounts Clerk. Report shortages, damages, or discrepancies to management immediately. Date and properly store products using FIFO (First In, First Out) inventory rotation. Maintain receiving logs and delivery records with temperature taking log. Stock Clerk Duties Organize and stock food, beverages, paper products, and cleaning supplies. Assist in maintaining par levels twice a week, to ensure accurate ordering.  Monitor inventory levels and notify supervisors when supplies need replenishment. Maintain cleanliness, check for proper temperature daily, organized storage rooms, refrigerators, and freezers. Rotate inventory to minimize waste and spoilage. Assist with monthly and annual inventory counts. Deliver supplies to kitchen and serving areas as needed. Process requisitions and deliver food and supplies to correct Campus units daily, checking for accuracy (pack size, quantity requested and correct item codes). Maintain security of storage areas within CAS, reporting any security and/or safety risks to management immediately. Will be called upon as situations arise (at any hour) to empty Dining Services cooler/freezer units to prevent loss of product/spoilage while securing food safety and sanitary storage conditions. Transportation Duties Transport or assign personnel to deliver food, goods, Catering equipment and supplies as needed by operations throughout CAS both campus-wide including off-campus functions. Ensure that all CAS vehicles are in proper working condition and related paperwork and decals are valid and tires, oil changes, operating fluids etc. are maintained consistently.  Vehicles are to be kept clean |& safely parked and secured in designated areas.  Ensure Monthly Vehicle Inspections are completed for all CAS vehicles on a Monthly basis. Preventive Maintenance of Equipment Perform routine inspections with Managers & Chefs of kitchen and food service equipment to ensure longevity & maintenance. Clean and maintain equipment according to manufacturer's recommendations. Replace basic wear items such as filters, gaskets, and light bulbs when appropriate. Report equipment malfunctions requiring repair. Maintain preventive maintenance schedules and records. (Example-Clean Ice Machine, Clean Cooler Coils, etc?.) at the end of every semester, or as needed. Alert supervisor  for reporting to maintenance personnel or outside service vendors for major repairs. Ensure equipment operates safely and efficiently. Monitor all coolers/freezers and enter onto log sheets daily.  Let management know if any issue arises, ASAP. Painting, lighting, and repairs in CAS areas.  Work with supervisor who will coordinate with campus Facilities, the submission of facility work orders. Monitor any build-up of mold/residual /standing water in cooler units and ice machines. Monthly maintenance of ice machines and all beverage ice dispensers, empty and clean ice machines. Monitor and ensure that drains are clean and properly working and are not clogged. Wash exterior of all CAS vehicles twice a semester or as needed. Interior should be cleaned once at the beginning and end of each semester or as needed. Safety and Sanitation Follow all food safety and sanitation regulations. Maintain compliance with OSHA and local health department standards. Use proper lifting techniques and personal protective equipment (PPE). Keep work areas clean and free of hazards. Dispose of waste according to established procedures. Tools and equipment used: Refrigeration units, scales, hand trucks, lift gates, pallets and pallet jacks, elevator, carts, cleaning equipment, BBQ grills, snow blowers, as well as propane air tanks. Assist in other areas as requested by management. Requirements: Qualifications: High school diploma or GED preferred. Previous experience in food service, receiving, warehouse, or inventory control, preferred. Basic mechanical aptitude for equipment maintenance. Ability to operate small hand tools and power equipment. Knowledge of food safety and sanitation practices. Pass ServSafe Certification. Ability to operate pallet jacks, carts, and other material handling equipment. Must always hold a valid NY State Driver's License and be able to operate all CAS Dining Service' vehicles with automatic and/or manual transmissions. Working Conditions: Commercial kitchen and food storage areas. Exposure to hot and cold temperatures. (-20 to 100 degrees F.) Moderate noise levels. Weekend, holiday, and evening work may be required. Physical Requirements: Frequently lift and carry up to 100 pounds. Stand, walk, bend, reach, sit, and climb for extended periods. Work in refrigerated, freezer, and kitchen environments. (-20 to 100 degrees F.) Ability to push and pull loaded carts and stock. Work with some chemical cleaning agents. Clean, neat and professional uniform, always. Must meet food handler standards. Additional Information: Department: Dining Services Reports to: Residential and Retail Dining Directors and Sr. Director of Dining Services Location: Residential and Retail Units Employment and Type: Non-Exempt, Full-Time 32 weeks/yr (coincides with academic calendar) 37.5 hours/week 6am - 2pm Monday - Friday Salary: $20.10/hour Compensation and Benefits: Medical, Dental, Vision, Life Insurances, Retirement, Annual Leave and Sick Leave, Savings Plan are available. Please note: This job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties, or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job.  Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time, with or without notice, based upon the needs of the operation. EEO STATEMENT: EEO employees are protected by federal laws, Presidential Executive Orders and other laws from discrimination on the basis of race, religion, color, sex (including pregnancy and gender identity), sexual orientation, parental status, national origin, age, disability, family medical history or genetic information, political affiliations, military service or any other non-merit-based factors.  These protections extend to all management practices and decisions, including recruitment and hiring practices, appraisal systems, promotions, and training and career development programs.  EEO employees are also protected against retaliation.  Consistent with federal laws, acts of retaliation against an employee who engages in a protected activity, whistle blowing, or the exercise of any appeal or grievance right provided by law, will not be tolerated.  In addition, consistent with the RESOLVED Program (Non-Retaliation Statement9, the EEOC will not tolerate retaliation against participation in RESOLVE. EEOC managers and supervisors are also reminded again of their responsibility to prevent, document and promptly address/correct harassing conduct in the workplace. Application Instructions: The application review process will begin immediately and will continue until a suitable candidate is found. Please provide: Resume Cover Letter References Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Cobleskill 106 Suffolk Circle, Cobleskill, NY 12043"
    },
    "https://cobleskill.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=202450": {
      "title": "Food Handler - CAS Dining Services at",
      "description": "SUNY Cobleskill\nJob Posting: Food Handler - CAS Dining Services at SUNY Cobleskill - #668 SUNY Cobleskill \n\tJob Posting: Food Handler - CAS Dining Services at SUNY Cobleskill - #668 Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Food Handler - CAS Dining Services at SUNY Cobleskill - #668 Category: CAS Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: CAS Locations: Cobleskill, NY Posted: Jul 10, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 202450 Share About SUNY Cobleskill: SUNY Cobleskill Auxiliary Services, (CAS) is a not-for-profit corporation committed to delivering quality services at competitive prices to the SUNY Cobleskill campus community.  CAS Provides outstanding services that collectively support students, faculty, staff, and guests while contributing to the local community.  Through expert customer service, CAS supports the pursuit of academic excellence, encourages personal growth, and cultivates sustainability, yielding superior quality of life for all. Job Description: JOB DESCRIPTION / ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS: Position requires the preparation and service of food and beverages. Requires the use and operation of food service/kitchen equipment and appliances. Operate point-of-sale system and follow all cashiering guidelines Perform duties as outlined in the Standard Operating Procedures. Must be able to read Possess and utilize organizational qualities Self-Starter Free of communicable diseases and protection of all open cuts, wounds, and skin abrasions ServSafe® Certified within one-year of hire Professional, neat, and clean appearance, wearing slip-resistant footwear and full uniform Respectful of co-workers and customers Must be customer-service minded with an emphasis on quality Must be able to work in a diverse environment. PRIMARY DUTIES: Food preparation, serving, cooking, cashiering, utility/dishroom ADDITIONAL WORK-RELATED INFORMATION: You may be called upon, at times, to work at related tasks, within your classification, not included in the above description. You may be required to temporarily work in a lower classification without change in pay rate. You may be requested to temporarily work on a job in a higher classification at your existing pay rate, however, you may refuse without fear of management condemnation. You may be scheduled to work at special functions, picnics, etc. held on- or off-campus, and to perform duties related to the above description. Work schedules, days off, job assignments, and unit assignments are subject to change and/or adjustment based upon the needs of the operation. Occasional evening and weekend work may be required, as job duties fluctuate. Requirements: Required: High School Diploma or equivalent Working Conditions: This job operates in a professional kitchen environment with many types of equipment. Physical Demands: The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully and safely perform the essential functions of this job. May be required to lift up to 50 pounds May be required to be on feet for duration of shift May be required to sit for duration of shift. Some bending and stretching may be required to place items on low and high shelves Possible exposure to extreme temperatures, slippery floors, and high humidity Work with some chemical cleaning agents The employee is frequently required to stand, walk, use hands and fingers to handle and feel, reach with hands and arms, communicate/give and receive information effectively. Additional Information: Department: Dining Services Reports to: Director of Residential Dining Location: Retail Unit Employment and Type: Non-Exempt, Full-Time 40 weeks/yr (coincides with academic calendar) 40 hours/week 3:30pm - 12:00m Sunday - Thursday Salary: $20.10/hour Compensation and Benefits: Medical, Dental, Vision, Life Insurances, Retirement, Annual Leave and Sick Leave, Savings Plan are available. Please note: This job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties, or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job.  Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time, with or without notice, based upon the needs of the operation. EEO STATEMENT: EEO employees are protected by federal laws, Presidential Executive Orders and other laws from discrimination on the basis of race, religion, color, sex (including pregnancy and gender identity), sexual orientation, parental status, national origin, age, disability, family medical history or genetic information, political affiliations, military service or any other non-merit-based factors.  These protections extend to all management practices and decisions, including recruitment and hiring practices, appraisal systems, promotions, and training and career development programs.  EEO employees are also protected against retaliation.  Consistent with federal laws, acts of retaliation against an employee who engages in a protected activity, whistle blowing, or the exercise of any appeal or grievance right provided by law, will not be tolerated.  In addition, consistent with the RESOLVED Program (Non-Retaliation Statement9, the EEOC will not tolerate retaliation against participation in RESOLVE. EEOC managers and supervisors are also reminded again of their responsibility to prevent, document and promptly address/correct harassing conduct in the workplace. Application Instructions: The application review process will begin immediately and will continue until a suitable candidate is found. Please provide: Resume Cover Letter References Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Cobleskill 106 Suffolk Circle, Cobleskill, NY 12043"
